WEBVTT

00:15:29.121 --> 00:15:32.204
So the expected value of
it might be negative,

00:15:32.371 --> 00:15:36.162
although when you look back
every big success you can

00:15:37.371 --> 00:15:38.412
trace to some irrationality.

00:15:39.204 --> 00:15:42.746
Well, that goes beautifully to one
of my favorite ideas of yours,

00:15:42.746 --> 00:15:47.537
that we look at successful people
and we learn from their habits,

00:15:47.537 --> 00:15:50.787
not realizing that we haven't compared
them with people who failed,

00:15:51.121 --> 00:15:52.621
who had many of the same habits.

00:15:53.954 --> 00:15:56.829
And I wanted to, I guess, ask
you a broader question,

00:15:56.829 --> 00:16:00.871
which is having put these kinds of
decision heuristics and cognitive biases